{"name":"Ecstasy","hex":"#c96138","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ecstasy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of ecstasy (“drug”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ecstasy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ecstasy (emotion)","blocks":[{"text":"Ecstasy is a subjective experience of total involvement of the subject with an object of their awareness. In classical Greek literature, it refers to removal of the mind or body \"from its normal place of function.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Rom%2C_Santa_Maria_della_Vittoria%2C_Die_Verz%C3%BCckung_der_Heiligen_Theresa_%28Bernini%29.jpg/330px-Rom%2C_Santa_Maria_della_Vittoria%2C_Die_Verz%C3%BCckung_der_Heiligen_Theresa_%28Bernini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecstasy_(emotion)"},{"title":"Religious ecstasy","blocks":[{"text":"Religious ecstasy is a purported form of altered state of consciousness characterized by greatly reduced external awareness and reportedly expanded interior mental and spiritual awareness, frequently accompanied by visions and emotional euphoria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Giuseppe_Bazzani_-_The_Ecstasy_of_St_Therese_-_WGA01527.jpg/330px-Giuseppe_Bazzani_-_The_Ecstasy_of_St_Therese_-_WGA01527.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Religious_ecstasy"},{"title":"Ecstasy (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ecstasy is a 1933 Czech erotic romantic drama film directed by Gustav Machatý and starring Hedy Lamarr, Aribert Mog, and Zvonimir Rogoz. Machatý won the award for Best Director for this film at the 1934 Venice Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/Extase_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.